      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Hisonotus notatus Eigenmann &amp; Eigenmann, 1889</li><li>Common name: Black Otocinclus</li><li>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2018)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/hisonotus_notatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: southeast Brazil. Requirements are the same as those of the Otocinclus species. A durable care.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1390",
      "html": "<p>South America: Brazil. Rivers of Rio de Janeiro State (including Macaé), Minas Gerais State, Espirito Santo State and Sao Paulo State.</p><p>Type locality: Rio de Janeiro State, Santa Cruz, rio Guandu, Santa Cruz farm - Emperor Pedro II's farm, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/hisonotus_notatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>From southeast Brazil some rare specimens could be imported, related to the popular Otocinclus species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/hisonotus_notatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>In its homeland Hisonotus ornatus inhabits waters infested with weeds.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/hisonotus_notatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The requirements for their maintenance do not differ from those of the Otocinclus species: good filtering and frequent water changes are the requirements for their well-being.</p>"
    },
    {
